@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Maze Explorer"; }
<div class="mb-4"><h1 class="hero-title">Maze Explorer</h1><p class="hero-subtitle">Find your way from S to E. Use the arrow keys or movement buttons.</p></div>
<div class="apple-card mb-5" data-maze><div class="maze-grid" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Maze. Use arrow keys to move." data-maze-grid></div><p role="status" class="mt-3" data-maze-status></p><div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2"><button type="button" class="btn-apple-secondary" data-move="up" aria-label="Move up">↑</button><button type="button" class="btn-apple-secondary" data-move="left" aria-label="Move left">←</button><button type="button" class="btn-apple-secondary" data-move="down" aria-label="Move down">↓</button><button type="button" class="btn-apple-secondary" data-move="right" aria-label="Move right">→</button><button type="button" class="btn-apple-secondary" data-maze-reset>Restart</button></div><p class="form-text mt-3">S = start · E = exit · solid cells = walls · outlined circle = you</p></div>
<details class="lesson-details"><summary>How it works</summary><div class="lesson-content"><p>A 2D array stores the map: 0 is a path, 1 is a wall, S is the start, and E is the exit. Every move checks the next row and column. Walls and map edges block movement. Reaching E completes the maze.</p></div></details>
